Jira Link: [[DB-382]](https://yugabyte.atlassian.net/browse/DB-382)
DB Version: **2.11.2.0-b83**

If user creates indexes with colocated = true or colocated =  false, query fails with 
```
db1=# create index idx1 on t1(name) WITH (colocated = true);
ERROR:  unrecognized parameter "colocated"
db1=# create index idx1 on t1(name) WITH (colocated = false);
ERROR:  unrecognized parameter "colocated" 
```

**Note**: Create index with default colocation is working fine.

**Steps**:
1. create database db1 with colocated = true;
2. \c db1;
3. create table table1(i int primary key, name text);
4. create index idx1 on table1(name) WITH colocated = false;



